DrugRef2 for CARLOS EMR — package notes
=======================================

DrugRef2 is the drug and drug-interaction reference service CARLOS queries over
XML-RPC when a prescription is written. Without it, prescription drug lookups
return no results.

Deployment
----------
It is deployed as a second web application inside the CARLOS Tomcat instance
rather than in a JVM of its own. On a single host that saves a second heap and
a second service to supervise; the isolation that matters is preserved by the
servlet container's per-application class loaders and by the two access gates
below. (The container-based carlos-podman deployment runs it in a separate
container, where the trade-off is different.)

Access control
--------------
DrugRef speaks UNAUTHENTICATED XML-RPC: anything that can reach
/drugref2/DrugrefService can query it. It is gated twice, and neither gate is
load-bearing on its own:

  1. nginx returns 404 for /drugref2 — the front door has no route to it.
  2. A RemoteCIDRValve in /etc/carlos-emr/tomcat/Catalina/localhost/drugref2.xml
     refuses any client whose address is not the host loopback.

`carlosctl check` probes the first of these from outside and fails if the
service is reachable through the front door.

Database
--------
DrugRef connects as its own `drugref` account, which holds privileges on the
drugref2 database only. Upstream's own configuration connects as root; on a
host where one MariaDB serves both applications, a drug-lookup service must not
hold a credential that can read the patient schema.

The drug dataset
----------------
The package loads the Health Canada Drug Product Database seed that ships with
CARLOS, but ONLY into an empty drugref2 database — reloading over a populated
one would discard updates a site has applied. The upstream seed creates its
tables as ENGINE=Aria; the package converts them to InnoDB immediately, because
a non-transactional table cannot take part in the backup's --single-transaction
snapshot and would otherwise be reported by every nightly backup.

Refresh or replace the dataset according to your own drug-data source and
licensing. Commercial Medi-Span interaction monographs need a licence key in
/etc/carlos-emr/drugref2.properties.

Removing it
-----------
Removing the package undeploys the context and restarts the EMR. The drugref2
database is left in place; drop it deliberately if you want it gone.
